<title>USA: KP&amp;L sees Mo. coal unit back Thurs morning.</title>
<headline>KP&amp;L sees Mo. coal unit back Thurs morning.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kansas City Power and Light Co's 670 megawatt Iatan coal-fired unit, shut early Tuesday, is expected to return to service early Thursday, the company said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The unit should be back up by tomorrow at six a.m. (0600 CST/1200 GMT),&quot; a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The unit was shut early Tuesday to repair a leak in a boiler feed pump.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
